    LOAN AGREEMENT

    January 14, 2021

    BETWEEN:

    1.1 MegaCorp USA, Inc., a Delaware corporation with its principal place of business located at 123 Main Street, Anytown, USA 12345 (hereinafter "Lender"),

    AND

    1.2 SmallBiz Inc., a California corporation with its principal place of business located at 456 Park Avenue, Smallville, CA 98765 (hereinafter "Borrower").

    WHEREAS, Lender desires to extend credit to Borrower; and
    WHEREAS, Borrower needs to borrow funds from Lender;
    NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants contained herein and for other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which is hereby acknowledged, the parties hereto agree as follows:

    1. LOAN TERMS

        1.1 The Lender shall extend to the Borrower a loan in the amount of Fifty Million Dollars ($50,000,000) (the "Principal Amount").

        1.2 The loan shall bear interest at the rate of eight percent (8%) per annum, payable semi-annually in arrears.

        1.3 The loan shall mature on January 14, 2026 (the "Maturity Date").

    2. INTEREST AND FEES

        2.1 The Borrower shall pay interest on the Principal Amount, calculated on the basis of a 360-day year, at the rate specified in Section 1.2, and shall pay such interest on the dates specified in Section 1.3.

        2.2 The Borrower shall pay all fees and expenses incurred in connection with the loan, including but not limited to, legal fees, processing fees, and any other fees or expenses as may be agreed upon in writing by the parties.

    3. DEFAULT AND REMEDIES

        3.1 If the Borrower fails to make any payment when due, or breaches any other provision of this Agreement, the Lender may declare all amounts owing under this Agreement immediately due and payable.

        3.2 The Lender shall have the right, at its option, to accelerate the repayment of the Principal Amount, accrued and unpaid interest, and any other amounts owing under this Agreement upon the occurrence of any event of default.

        3.3 Upon any acceleration of the Principal Amount, the Lender shall have the right to institute any legal or equitable proceedings against the Borrower to recover all amounts owing under this Agreement.

        3.4 In the event of any foreclosure or other sale of the Borrower's assets, the Lender shall be entitled to be paid out of the proceeds of such sale before any other creditor, in an amount equal to the Principal Amount, accrued and unpaid interest, and any other amounts owing under this Agreement.

    4. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES

        4.1 The Borrower represents and warrants that it has full power and authority to enter into this Agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder.

        4.2 The Borrower represents and warrants that the execution and delivery of this Agreement and the performance of its obligations hereunder have been duly authorized by all necessary corporate action on its part.

    5. GOVERNING LAW

    This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York.

    IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties hereto have executed this Loan Agreement as of the date first above written.

